  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 310 AM EDT Thu Jun 25 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will build over the eastern US this weekend, \ncentering itself just to our west/northwest by early next week. \nRising heights will allow for temperatures to warm into the 90s \nareawide this weekend (outside higher elevation locations of \nnortheast GA). Increasing humidity will help push heat indices \nover 100 by Sunday, with heat index values potentially approaching\nor exceeding 105 degrees early next week across parts of the \narea. This general synoptic pattern appears likely to continue \ninto the middle to end of next week, with ensemble guidance in \nreasonably good agreement through the period. Ridging will likely \nsuppress precipitation chances, though can't completely rule out a\npop-up shower or storm most afternoons with daytime heating.",
